SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: How Hip-Hop Built an Empire
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 13 spots left\nS
 tatus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/even
 ts/203633\n\n6:30PM Reception\, 7:00PM Discussion\n\nWhat is it about hip-
 hop that has transformed generations of artists into some of the world’s
  most influential entrepreneurs\, tastemakers\, and cultural forces? Join 
 us for a ’Quin Chat exploring the evolution of the hip-hop artist from p
 erformer to mogul - and how a genre born from creative expression has beco
 me a powerful engine for business\, innovation\, and cultural influence. F
 rom fashion and record labels to food and beverage\, technology\, media\, 
 and beyond\, the conversation will examine how artists have built expansiv
 e ecosystems around their creativity while reshaping the industries they e
 nter. \n\nNeil Martinez Belkin\, New York Times bestselling author\, wi
 ll be joined in conversation by Boston native Dart Adams\, an acclaimed jo
 urnalist\, historian\, researcher\, lecturer\, and author. Together\, the
 y will explore the entrepreneurial mindset behind hip-hop’s most influen
 tial figures\, the relationship between cultural credibility and commercia
 l success\, and how the genre continues to redefine what it means to be an
  artist\, and a mogul\, today.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserve
 d for members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be ser
 ved. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior 
 to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203633
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
