SUMMARY:Author's Circle Book Club: "Safekeeping" by Claudia Hinz
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 11 spots left\nS
 tatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/20362
 9\n\nThis October\, settle into the season with Safekeeping by Claudia Hin
 z\, a sweeping and deeply moving novel about family\, memory\, and the sec
 rets we carry across generations. Set against the rugged beauty of Norther
 n California\, the story follows the intertwined lives of three women as l
 ong-held truths begin to surface\, revealing the complicated bonds between
  mothers and daughters and the choices that shape a family over time.\n\nA
 tmospheric and richly layered\, Safekeeping explores belonging\, resilienc
 e\, and the ways our past continues to shape the present. With its evocati
 ve setting and intimate exploration of family relationships\, it is a fitt
 ing fall read—and an ideal choice for readers drawn to thoughtful\, char
 acter-driven stories that linger long after the final page.\n\nJoined by a
 uthor Claudia Hinz\, the evening will offer a closer look at the inspirati
 on behind Safekeeping\, its characters\, and the themes woven throughout t
 he novel. Members will have the opportunity to hear directly from Hinz and
  explore the story through an intimate conversation that brings the book -
  and the world within it - to life.\n\n*This event is complimentary and re
 served for members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will b
 e served.We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours pr
 ior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203629
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
